From: SamuriHL <samurihl@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vh265: flush the enhancement layer when the base layer ends

A dual-layer (Dolby Vision FEL/MEL) stream-mode pair schedules the
enhancement layer only when the base layer's parser hands over to it
(switch_dvlayer_flag). When the player ends the stream (AMSTREAM_SET_EOS)
the base layer takes DEC_RESULT_EOS and flushes its own reorder buffer,
but keeps sched, and its run_ready returns 0 from then on: the slave
never runs again, and its last pictures stay in its reorder buffer. The
Dolby Vision path then holds the base pictures that did come out ("bl
wait el") - the last pictures of a FEL file or disc segment never show
(FEL_test_for_AVS.m2ts: two).

Flush the slave from the base layer's EOS branch, exactly as the "no el
anymore" path in the ISR already does, and before the base layer so
every base picture finds its enhancement picture queued.

---
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
@@ -14738,6 +14738,26 @@
 		hevc_print(hevc, PRINT_FLAG_VDEC_STATUS,
 			"%s: end of stream, last dec poc %d => 0x%pf\n",
 			__func__, hevc->curr_POC, pic);
+		/* Dual-layer: the enhancement layer is scheduled only when this
+		 * layer's parser hands over to it, which never happens again once
+		 * this layer has ended - so flush it here, as the "no el anymore"
+		 * path in the ISR does, and before the base layer, so every base
+		 * picture that goes out finds its enhancement picture queued. */
+		if (vdec->slave && vdec->slave->private) {
+			struct hevc_state_s *hevc_el =
+				(struct hevc_state_s *)vdec->slave->private;
+			struct PIC_s *el_pic;
+
+			check_pic_decoded_error(hevc_el,
+				hevc_el->pic_decoded_lcu_idx);
+			el_pic = get_pic_by_POC(hevc_el, hevc_el->curr_POC);
+			hevc_el->curr_POC = INVALID_POC;
+			hevc_el->m_pocRandomAccess = MAX_INT;
+			flush_output(hevc_el, el_pic);
+			hevc_el->decoded_poc = INVALID_POC;
+			hevc_el->decoding_pic = NULL;
+			hevc_print(hevc, 0, "end of stream: flushed el\n");
+		}
 		flush_output(hevc, pic);
 		/* dummy vf with eos flag to backend */
 		notify_v4l_eos(hw_to_vdec(hevc));
